WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:05.189
The hierarchy of power in the DC universe
is… disputed, at this point.

00:00:05.189 --> 00:00:10.269
"The hierarchy of power in the DC universe
is about to change."

00:00:10.269 --> 00:00:14.110
If your perception of "Black Adam" is based
on the ad campaign and Dwayne Johnson's hype

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:16.990
machine, you'd think it was the greatest thing
since sliced bread.

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:19.970
But reality appears to be a little bit more
complicated.

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:24.359
While it's far from a trainwreck of a film,
"Black Adam" is also far from the paradigm-shifting

00:00:24.359 --> 00:00:25.970
film it was made out to be.

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:30.679
Even with the inclusion of the Justice Society
of America, Henry Cavill's Superman, and Johnson

00:00:30.679 --> 00:00:35.540
finally portraying DC Comics' Teth-Adam after
years of waiting, people didn't exactly rush

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:37.500
to the theater to check the movie out.

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:41.280
While it claimed the top spot at the weekend
box office a few times in its run, "Black

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:44.960
Adam's" performance has been relatively muted
– especially compared to the much bigger

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:46.980
run of "Black Panther: Wakanda Forever."

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:52.690
"Black Adam" is resting just under the $400
million mark in terms of worldwide box office gross.

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:54.350
In isolation, that's an impressive number.

00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:58.239
For a superhero movie starring one of the
world's biggest movie stars, it's a little

00:00:58.239 --> 00:00:59.239
bit sus.

00:00:59.239 --> 00:01:03.570
Taken in context with the movie's reported
$200 million budget, as well as a reported

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:07.670
$100 million marketing campaign, the amount
of money "Black Adam" has brought in starts

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:09.260
seeming pretty small.

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:11.280
But is it actually going to lose money?

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:15.490
That's a point being hotly contested by industry
reporters, the studio, and the movie's star

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:17.470
producer, Dwayne Johnson himself.

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:21.820
That debate has a new wrinkle now with a bombshell
report that Johnson's camp leaked misleading

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:26.340
financial info about "Black Adam" on purpose,
to help spin the movie's performance as positive

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:27.460
– and profitable.

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:30.600
Here's what the rumor mill has churned up
about this situation so far.

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:35.649
"These powers are not a gift, but a curse."

00:01:35.649 --> 00:01:40.450
On December 7, 2022, Deadline explained that
contrary to other reports citing "Black Adam"

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:44.110
as a financial failure, the movie stands to
rake in some profit after all.

00:01:44.110 --> 00:01:48.880
The rough window Deadline reported puts the
film's projected earnings between $52 and

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:53.049
$72 million – a number which allegedly includes
merchandise related to the film.

00:01:53.049 --> 00:01:57.240
Less than a week later, however, former editor
of The Hollywood Reporter Matt Belloni came

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:00.930
forward with a surprising claim that appeared
to contradict those numbers.

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:04.930
Not only will "Black Adam" not bring in millions
for Warner Bros. Discovery, but according

00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:09.349
to Belloni's sources, Dwayne Johnson 's team
purposely leaked false financial information

00:02:09.349 --> 00:02:10.429
to the press.

00:02:10.429 --> 00:02:12.503
On the industry newsletter Puck, Belloni wrote,

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:24.959
Belloni clarified that no one on Johnson's
team has yet admitted to any such leak.

00:02:24.959 --> 00:02:28.840
Instead, he claims that individuals within
Warner Bros. Discovery have expressed their

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:32.670
belief that Johnson put those misleading numbers
out there, leading to outlets like Deadline

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:35.760
reporting on it and propagating a positive
spin for the movie.

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:39.840
If this report from Matt Belloni is true,
it raises questions about the ramifications

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:44.000
for the movie's future in the DC universe,
as well as Dwayne Johnson's relationship with

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:45.377
Warner Bros. Discovery.

00:02:45.377 --> 00:02:49.319
Before this rumor came to light, we learned
that major shake-ups are on the way for DC,

00:02:49.319 --> 00:02:52.310
and the "Black Adam" brand might have a lot
to worry about.

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:58.019
On December 7, 2022, The Hollywood Reporter
noted that under the guidance of James Gunn

00:02:58.019 --> 00:03:01.950
and Peter Safran, the DC film and television
slate is supposedly up for some big changes.

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:07.280
"Wonder Woman 3" has been canned, Jason Momoa
could switch from Aquaman to Lobo, and Henry

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:11.280
Cavill may already be done as Superman even
though he just returned to the role.

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:15.540
THR also reported that the first Black Adam's
financial woes could take a sequel off the

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:19.930
table entirely, regardless of what Johnson
– or the movie's tantalizing post-credits

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:21.297
scene – might have you believe.

00:03:21.492 --> 00:03:23.534
So is the movie a total failure?

00:03:23.534 --> 00:03:27.659
That's up in the air – but if it was successful,
we probably wouldn't have to ask.

00:03:27.659 --> 00:03:31.430
For now, the big question is whether or not
"Black Adam" is really going to turn a profit,

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:33.269
or if it's doomed to stay in the red.

00:03:33.624 --> 00:03:35.234
"I kneel before no one."

